    {
      "title": "Calculating Bands",
      "slug": "calculating-bands",
      "displayOrder": 1,
      "legacy": {
        "itemId": 648,
        "lessonOrder": 1
      },
      "blocks": [
        {
          "components": [
            {
              "type": "richText",
              "html": "Calculating stitches for neckbands or front bands for cardigans is mysterious for many knitters.<br>We are often instructed to “pick up 2 stitches for every 3 rows” or “pick up 3 stitches for every 4 rows”. You may be surprised that these methods are often quite inaccurate.<br>The general convention is to try one of these “rules” and rip out the band and try again until we are satisfied.<br>Here’s a better way. In this tutorial we will explore 4 methods of calculating the number of stitches to pick up and determine the BEST way.<br>",
              "legacyComponentId": 8461,
              "order": 1
            },
            {
              "type": "video",
              "vimeoId": "151857646",
              "title": "Calculating Bands",
              "legacyComponentId": 8462,
              "order": 2
            }
          ],
          "title": "Using Math",
          "slug": "using-math",
          "order": 1,
          "legacy": {
            "assignId": 5701,
            "blockType": "HTML"
          }
        },
        {
          "components": [
            {
              "type": "richText",
              "html": "Let Knit it Now Calculate your band Pick Up.<br><div class=\"videopopup\" data-videotitle=\"Band Pickup Tool for Machine Knitters\" data-vimeoid=\"345981696\">\r\n\t\t<figure><figcaption align=\"center\"><br><i class=\"fa fa-youtube-play fa-2x learn\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> How to use the tool</figcaption><img class=\"img-thumbnail\" src=\"https://i.vimeocdn.com/video/795899429-3257f6fa737aa58d0382d40c680e25ec6eea1dea3271cff16ff5abc28ca8619f-d_1280x720?r=pad\"></figure>\r\n\t\t<div class=\"imagecenter text-center\"><button class=\"btn btn-sm\"><i class=\"fa fa-youtube-play fa-2x learn\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i></button></div>\t\t\r\n</div>\r\n",
              "legacyComponentId": 8465,
              "order": 1
            }
          ],
          "title": "Knit it Now Tool",
          "slug": "knit-it-now-tool",
          "order": 2,
