    {
      "title": "Off the Machine",
      "slug": "off-the-machine",
      "displayOrder": 2,
      "legacy": {
        "itemId": 682,
        "lessonOrder": 2
      },
      "blocks": [
        {
          "components": [
            {
              "type": "richText",
              "html": "<style>\r\n.flex-container {\r\ndisplay: flex;\r\njustify-content: center;\r\n}\r\n\r\n.flex-child:first-child {\r\nmargin-right: 20px;\r\nborder: 1px solid;\r\npadding: 20px;\r\nmargin-bottom: 20px;\r\n}\r\n\r\n.flex-child2 {\r\nmargin-right: 20px;\r\nborder: 1px solid;\r\npadding: 20px;\r\nmargin-bottom: 20px;\r\n}\r\n\r\n@media (max-width: 800px) {\r\n.flex-container {\r\nflex-direction: column;\r\n}\r\n\r\n</style>\r\n<span class=\"yellow_highlight\">There is no rule that says everything needs to be done on the machine.</span>  Sometimes picking up a crochet hook or hand knitting needles can be rewarding, especially in finishing hems and edges of our knitting.<br>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>\r\nA band of single crochet stitches may be just the finish you need.</li><br>\r\n<li>Pick up and knit <a data-GlossaryId=\"694\" class=\"glossaryhelp\">Garter Stitch <i class=\"fa fa-question-circle\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i></a> (knit every row) or <a data-GlossaryId=\"603\" class=\"glossaryhelp\">Seed Stitch / Moss Stitch <i class=\"fa fa-question-circle\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i></a> (alternating k1, p1)</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\nEither way, remember gauge. You don't want to stretch out the front edge of your sweater. For example garter stitch knits much wider than stockinette.<br>\r\nYou can always swatch in your band stitch technique and do the math, Or use the edge of your gauge swatch and experiment till you get it just right.<br><div class=\"flex-container\">\r\n<div class=\"flex-child\"><figure><img src=\"/challenge/images/v2/100/crochet_band.jpg\"><figcaption align=\"center\"><br>Rows of single crochet</figcaption>\r\n</figure>\r\n\r\n\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"flex-child2\">\t<figure><img src=\"/challenge/images/v2/100/garter_band.jpg\"><figcaption align=\"center\"><br>Garter Stitch</figcaption>\r\n</figure>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>",
              "legacyComponentId": 8821,
              "order": 1
            }
          ],
          "title": "Hand Finishing",
          "slug": "hand-finishing",
          "order": 1,
          "legacy": {
